  title: THE FOUNDRY FIRE
  description: 'My Pontiff, a fire tore through a foundry beside our chapel in the
    Crucible. The flames are out, but the smiths'' guild is at war with itself: the
    master blames careless apprentices, the apprentices blame the master''s greed.
    Whoever helps them now will have the Crucible''s gratitude, and its anvils.'
